{"book":{"id":"book-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin","slug":"divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin","title":"Divided Mastery: Slave Hiring in the American South","authors":[{"id":"person-jonathan-d-martin","name":"Jonathan D. Martin"}],"isbn13":["9780674011496"],"subjects":["History"],"topics":["Slavery & Emancipation","Courts & Trials","Labor, Work & Organizing","Family, Childhood & Adoption"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Divided%20Mastery%3A%20Slave%20Hiring%20in%20the%20American%20South%20Jonathan%20D.%20Martin","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Divided%20Mastery%3A%20Slave%20Hiring%20in%20the%20American%20South%20Jonathan%20D.%20Martin","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Divided%20Mastery%3A%20Slave%20Hiring%20in%20the%20American%20South%20Jonathan%20D.%20Martin","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Divided%20Mastery%3A%20Slave%20Hiring%20in%20the%20American%20South%20Jonathan%20D.%20Martin","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6035831W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-lincoln-prize-civil-war-era-gettysburg-college-previous-winners-of-the-gilder-lehrman-lincoln-pr","source-open-library-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin","source-open-library-summary-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin"],"publicationYear":2004,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/412109-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":24,"criticalRenown":62,"controversy":12,"llmAffinity":62,"affinityResidual":-11.13,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.78,"controversy":0.72,"llmAffinity":0.84},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"archival-research","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"\"Divided Mastery explores a curiously neglected aspect of the history of American slavery: the rental of slaves. Though few slaves escaped being rented out at some point in their lives, this is the first book to describe the practice and its effects on both slaves and the peculiar institution.\" \"Martin reveals how the unique triangularity of slave hiring created slaves with two masters, thus transforming the customary polarity of master-slave relationships. Drawing upon slaveholders' letters, slave narratives, interviews with former slaves, legislative petitions, and court records, Divided Mastery ultimately reveals that slave hiring's significance was paradoxical.\" \"The practice bolstered the system of slavery by facilitating its spread into the western territories, by democratizing access to slave labor, and by promoting both production and speculation with slave capital. But at the same time, slaves used hiring to their advantage, finding in it crucial opportunities to shape their work and family lives, to bring owners and hirers into conflict with each other, and to destabilize the system of bondage.\"--BOOK JACKET.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Employment","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Slavery","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Slaves","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-divided-mastery-slave-hiring-in-the-american-south-jonathan-d-martin"},{"source":"open_library